# robonix/system/scene/find — resolve a natural-language reference to the
# object or objects it could mean, or say it cannot.
#
# Replaces the list-everything-and-pick pattern. Measured on this stack,
# list_objects went from 921 B with two objects to 13.9 KB with thirty-four,
# and with eight chairs present the planner picked one on no basis and drove
# there. This returns at most `k` short rows and, when they cannot be
# separated, a question instead of a choice.
#
# Constraints are not blended. `cls` is a vocabulary match, `region` is a
# point-in-polygon test, and each relation is a lookup in the scene graph
# Scene already maintains — so "in the kitchen" is answered yes or no rather
# than scored, and cannot be outweighed by wording.

# Free-form residue: whatever the description says that the structured
# fields below do not capture. May be empty.
string text
# Optional class filter, e.g. "chair". Matched against the detector's
# vocabulary and any operator label.
string cls
# Optional region name. Resolved against the saved polygons.
string region
# Optional relations the target must stand in, e.g. near/sofa. Only
# relations Scene maintains are accepted; anything else is refused rather
# than silently dropped, because dropping a constraint changes the answer.
RelationConstraint[] relations
# Optional set predicate over the survivors: "closest" or "farthest".
# Cannot be a relation — a superlative depends on the candidate set, which
# depends on the query.
string predicate
# Reject candidates below this detection confidence. 0 disables.
float64 min_confidence
# Maximum candidates to return. 0 → service default (5).
int32 k
---
# unique | ambiguous | empty
string verdict
Candidate[] candidates
# Score gap between the top two. 1.0 when there is only one candidate.
float64 margin
# When ambiguous: a question naming what actually separates the candidates,
# phrased to be spoken. Empty otherwise.
string question
# Which constraint emptied the set, when one did: cls | region | relation |
# confidence. Lets a caller say "none in the kitchen; there are two in the
# bedroom" instead of "not found".
string narrowed_by
string detail
string map_id
float64 stamp_unix
